# Scratch output of a release run, wiped at the start of the next one. Nothing
# here is worth keeping — though note "rebuildable" only goes so far: a rebuild
# produces a *different* binary, with a new signature timestamp, cdhash and
# notarization ticket. It can't reproduce a DMG that has already shipped.
build/

# Shipped builds, kept precisely because they can't be reproduced. Deliberately
# not in git: a DMG is already compressed, so git can't delta it and would store
# every release at full size forever. The binaries live here and on the release
# page; RELEASES.md carries the hashes that identify them.
dist/

# Signing configuration, kept out of the repo so it carries no account details.
# Both have a tracked .example alongside them; copy each and fill in your team
# ID. Neither is needed to build unsigned — only to sign or release.
#
# Note Signing.xcconfig itself IS tracked and sets nothing: it optionally
# includes the file below, so a fresh clone builds with no setup. A missing base
# configuration reference is a hard build error, not a warning.
Signing.local.xcconfig
scripts/ExportOptions.plist

# Xcode
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
.DS_Store
